  "id": "one-case-may-prove-a-batch-of-requirements",
  "title": "One case may prove a batch of requirements",
  "requirement": "The case policy says one case per accepted behaviour and allows one verified run to prove several requirements while the case keeps its primary reqId; case_gate passes a task covering three reqIds behind one verified automated case and still blocks an unverified one, with the case schema unchanged.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "verified",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "plugins/test-cases/test/batch-gate.test.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node --test plugins/test-cases/test/batch-gate.test.mjs",
  "steps": [
    "assert SECTION_FULL and SECTION_INTAKE carry the one-case-per-behaviour rule and allow several requirements, and the module header dropped 'one case per observed requirement'",
    "write one verified automated case linked to a task that covers REQ-001..REQ-003 and call case_gate(taskId): ok true, no blockers",
    "add an unverified automated case and a documented-only unverified case: the first blocks, the second never does"
  ],
  "expected": "The test exits 0; the pre-P5 module does not export the policy sections and the negative control expect-pre-fix fails on the fixed text.",
